Correct the carry-over docs where the reviews found them wrong or silent

All three post-implementation reviewers checked the docs against the
code. This fixes what they found.

docs/command-ordering.md:
- Lists the differences from one-at-a-time processing that were
  missing: a command after a stop that cancelled the only play it named
  gets 404 where a fading sound would have answered; voice_fade_out
  cancelling a voice's only play ends the voice at once, so a play into
  it during the would-be fade starts at full volume; a play whose load
  fails could be reached while it loaded, so commands naming only it
  succeed; a windowed play makes its voice streamed only once it starts,
  so a speed or seek for that voice can apply to its other sounds while
  the windowed play loads; a carried volume applies to a windowed play
  though a volume after it starts does not.
- Says a carried seek into an undecoded part of a cold file plays
  silence until the decode reaches it, where a play's own
  start_position_ms waits for it.
- Says a play's load may wait for one of the four load slots, that a
  voice ends with the last of its plays to fail or be cancelled, and
  that /status/voices and active_voices include voices held open by a
  loading play.
- Drops claims that were false ("handle_command stays the one place a
  command takes effect") and wording tied to history ("as before", "as
  they always have", "written before the loop is restructured"), and
  says the MQTT reproduction was run by hand with results in bugs.md.

Elsewhere:
- commands.md: a later command naming only a cancelled play gets "not
  found".
- http-api.md: active_voices in /status and /metrics counts voices held
  open by a loading play.
- troubleshooting.md: a cancelled play is logged at INFO, with both
  reasons quoted, and "a stop already cancelled the play" is listed as
  a cause of "No sample matches the selector".
- voice-management.md: a voice also ends when the last of its plays
  fails or is cancelled without any starting.
- architecture.md: the Voice struct shows loading_plays (and not a
  fade_state it does not have); the source tree lists pending_plays.rs.
- README: the developer docs table links command-ordering.md.
- bugs.md: the measurement table header says 2.1.0-rc.1, the re-run
  results name the extra gaps they cover, and two paragraphs are
  rewrapped.
- CHANGELOG: quotes the voice commands' not-found messages exactly, and
  the panicked-load entry says it got the 409 of a cancelled load.
- Code comments: CommandErrorKind::Cancelled covers stops and shutdown,
  not only stopall/fadeall; the CommandScheduler doc no longer says
  every command goes through handle_command or that a load starts at
  once.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
